Q4. Write a program to input any alphabetic and check whether it is vowels or consonants .
A).
import java.util.Scanner;
public class TernaryPractice {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

      System.out.print("Enter an alphabet: ");
        char ch2 = sc.next().charAt(0);
        char lower = Character.toLowerCase(ch2);
        String vowelCheck = (lower == 'a' || lower == 'e' || lower == 'i' || lower == 'o' || lower == 'u')
                ? "Vowel" : "Consonant";
        System.out.println(ch2 + " is: " + vowelCheck);
    }
}

Q5. Write a program to input to any character and check whether it is alphabet or digit or any special character.
A).

import java.util.Scanner;
public class TernaryPractice {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

      System.out.print("Enter any character: ");
        char ch3 = sc.next().charAt(0);
        String type = Character.isLetter(ch3) ? "Alphabet"
                : Character.isDigit(ch3) ? "Digit"
                : "Special Character";
        System.out.println(ch3 + " is: " + type);

        sc.close();

    }
}
